  "query_preview": "..A dry flow aloft will set up over northern Arizona\nover the coming week, a blessed relief from TOO much rain over \nthe past few days.\n\nThe remainder of today through Tuesday...A weak high pressure \nsystem will move across Arizona. As a result, look for light and \nvariable winds, a bit warmer temperatures and generally clear \nskies. Even so, use caution when driving as many low water \ncrossings will still be flooded or otherwise inundated with water.\n\nOn Wednesday and Thursday...A weak and dry shortwave trough will \nbrush the area. Not much impact with this system except for a \nslight dip in high temperatures, variable high clouds and locally\ngusty west to northwest winds at 5-15 mph gusting to around 25 \nmph. Those higher gust will be located over the mountain areas \nfrom over the White Mountains and Mogollon Rim to the New Mexico \nborder.\n\nFrom Friday into Monday...High pressure will build over the \nsouthwest states with warming daytime temperatures and surface \npressure gradients that will favor north to northeast breezes at \n10-20 mph. But perhaps the most important message, continued dry.\n\nBeyond Monday...Chances for showers return but at this time look\nlikes a minimal threat compared to our most recent experience.",
